{"id": "EUVD-2026-81946", "enisaUuid": "6f4cb640-9400-3ee5-903f-f4a9680798bb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nocteontx2-af: fix NULL deref in NIX TM tree debugfs read path\n\nrvu_dbg_nix_tm_tree_display() dereferences pfvf->sq_ctx without\nchecking whether the SQ context has been allocated. Reading\n/sys/kernel/debug/octeontx2/nix/tm_tree for a NIX LF whose transmit\nqueues are not set up triggers a kernel oops.\n\nGuard the read path the same way rvu_dbg_nix_tm_tree_write() already\ndoes and return -EINVAL with a seq_file message when sq_ctx is NULL.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:57:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fb736d733b0a60377cf53010571c261886446fd5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/537e11a1700f64dc6754108f0e1333ad63d4f548", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fdf7358e2688f12eff41290bc45030b7aff0845e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ec65631bd5ec251cdf67a4919fac7a3149a6e235"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90085", "GHSA-m9hw-68r8-5833"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cb1b21f-201c-3677-a2bc-993f783f227a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "2ee3df69-f3a9-3e58-921b-cb5d7d941ad3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "3ddc0780-8cb6-3e0e-b16e-d8c042f3c409", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b907194a5d5bcd3b01d28d095f6a4d9fcd9c5354 <fdf7358e2688f12eff41290bc45030b7aff0845e"}, {"id": "6e9ef4de-7346-339c-9d28-a5fea6d6eae2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "721ba59b-fa39-3c5f-8692-dc0241d49d8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b907194a5d5bcd3b01d28d095f6a4d9fcd9c5354 <ec65631bd5ec251cdf67a4919fac7a3149a6e235"}, {"id": "7cd4f7e7-